  "about": "The sync secret's rule (Accounts AC7). Accepted: a PIN of 4 to 6 ASCII digits [0-9], or a passphrase of 8 characters or more. A secret made only of ASCII digits is a PIN, so any other digit count is pinTooShort / pinTooLong. Anything else under 8 characters is passphraseTooShort; the empty string is empty. Characters are Unicode code points (Dart: runes.length), nothing is trimmed, and other scripts' digits are not PIN digits. A PIN is pinTooSimple when every digit is the same, when it is a run of consecutive digits up or down (no wrapping from 9 to 0), or when two digits take turns (1212, 12121). expected is null when the secret is accepted.",
