  "strengthAbout": "syncSecretStrength (Phase 7, M7.5). A PIN (only ASCII digits) is its length × log2(10) bits, level \"pin\". A passphrase is the larger of: words (split on whitespace and -_.,;:+, those of 3 or more code points) × log2(7776) when there are 3 or more such words, else 0; and (code points × log2(pool)) / 2, pool = 26 if a-z, +26 if A-Z, +10 if 0-9, +33 if ASCII punctuation or space, +100 if any code point above 0x7f. A passphrase whose lowercase is on the common list, or with 3 distinct code points or fewer, is at most 10 bits. bits is rounded down; level is weak under 40, fair under 50, strong from 50; seconds = round(2^bits / 2 / 10000), at most 1e15.",
